From: Loong <1031313955@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] configs: nokia_xg-040g-mf: enable minimal HTTP recovery server

Same three options 950 turns on for xg-040g-md: the TCP stack and the httpd
command from 202, plus the cyclic framework it uses to keep the panel LEDs
blinking during a flash write (the SPI-NAND layer calls schedule() once per
page, which is what drives it).

The server itself is board-independent -- it lives in net/httpd.c and is
built into U-Boot core -- so enabling it here is all this board needs.

Must sort after 402-add-nokia-xg-040g-mf.patch, which is the patch that
creates this defconfig in the first place.

--- a/configs/an7583_nokia_xg-040g-mf_defconfig
+++ b/configs/an7583_nokia_xg-040g-mf_defconfig
@@ -41,6 +41,9 @@ CONFIG_CMD_TFTPSRV=y
 CONFIG_CMD_MTD_NAND_WRITE_TEST=y
 CONFIG_CMD_PART=y
 CONFIG_CMD_TFTPSRV=y
+CONFIG_PROT_TCP=y
+CONFIG_CMD_HTTPD=y
+CONFIG_CYCLIC=y
 CONFIG_CMD_RARP=y
 CONFIG_CMD_CDP=y
 CONFIG_CMD_SNTP=y
